#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:5
#: 10c9da8a237244fe98eae86ca1d41e71
msgid "Initial Tuning Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:8
#: 2d2694e57fae4818a5869b9cf6565e3c
msgid "Pilot's preparation for first flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:10
#: 222d02f42e3b4eb1a761a079101798e6
msgid ""
"The first takeoff of an untuned multirotor is the most dangerous seconds "
"of the aircraft’s life. This is where the aircraft could be very unstable"
" causing a sudden increase in power when then results in the aircraft "
"jumping into the air, or it may be so poorly tuned that you have "
"insufficient control over the aircraft once it is airborne. The pilot "
"should be extremely diligent during the tuning flights to avoid a "
"situation that could result in injury or damage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:12
#: 206ae38204ce4637ae2d9200a50700ac
msgid ""
"There are several things that the pilot can do to minimise the risk "
"during the early tuning process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:14
#: 5cd09cf4d89c4a9bb7d8b59e3528f6ca
msgid ""
"The pilot should conduct a motor number and orientation check (see "
":ref:`Checking the motor numbering with the Mission Planner Motor test "
"<connect-escs-and-motors_testing_motor_spin_directions>`). Care should be"
" taken to ensure that the correct frame type is selected. Incorrect frame"
" type can result in a very fast yaw rotation or complete loss of control."
" Take note of the output percentage required to spin the propellers and "
"ensure that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:16
#: e5d06840a8db4f6eb6177156ba4f29ef
msgid ""
":ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` is set high enough to spin the motors "
"cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:17
#: 42125e2940534888a0397e6df240eb61
msgid ""
":ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` is set high enough to spin the motors "
"with a minimal level of thrust."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:19
#: 540ed4ddc24b43888ff800d467322a87
msgid ""
"All flights after a significant tuning change should be done in "
"Stabilize. Stabilize provides the pilot with significantly more control "
"over the aircraft in the event that the attitude controllers are "
"unstable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:20
#: 30d66527e629489bb86d563091d59085
msgid ""
"The pilot should not take off in AltHold until the altitude controller "
"has been tested in flight. This should be done by taking off in Stabilize"
" and switching to Alt Hold. While Alt Hold is rarely a problem unless the"
" aircraft has a very low hover throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:21
#: a183b8d1541b467e8bc8dba8359c901f
msgid ""
"For the initial flights the pilot should ensure that these parameters are"
" set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:23
#: 1e1bb3c309e24614a7d3fc6bddb115a5
msgid ":ref:`ATC_THR_MIX_MAN <ATC_THR_MIX_MAN>` to 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:24
#: 01da28660f804ff5a53a87bb7fda8649
msgid ""
":ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>` to 0.25 (or lower than the "
"expected hover throttle)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:26
#: 69e387ed6a0b4e1caecfa2042e91a2a0
msgid ""
"Use a radio and calibrate the radio correctly (see :ref:`common-radio-"
"control-calibration`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:27
#: 07480191f910492f9049a33c6ab4c081
msgid ""
"Configure an Emergency Stop Motors switch and test it (see "
":ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:28
#: 3d9afa762be14bbea53c07cb5c7a3bda
msgid ""
"Do tuning flights in low-wind condition and normal weather (no rain and "
"between 15°C/59°F and 25°C/77°F)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:29
#: d537e219d1b74b76a53d1cd76df02076
msgid ""
"Practice STABILIZE flight in simulator or on a low-end drone first, you "
"should be confident to be able to takeoff and land with your untuned "
"aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:33
#: c30df894d10b49c28f38819f755ed27a
msgid "First Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:35
#: b6fb03d5a0b44ad6be98f5d8a5237822
msgid ""
"The first take off is the most dangerous time for any multirotor. Care "
"must be taken to ensure the aircraft is not destroyed in the first "
"seconds of flight and nobody is injured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:37
#: fcda6386125b4250a335269bd2636366
msgid "**Ensure that all spectators are at a safe distance**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:38
#: 0640842044294618a65ed2c3a5d14928
msgid "**Ensure the pilot is at a safe distance and position**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:39
#: 3469bc3f978541938e2e19e1f4614acf
msgid ""
"The pilot should refresh themselves on the method used to disarm the "
"aircraft (using :ref:`Auxiliary Functions <common-auxiliary-functions>` "
"for Motor Interlock or Arm/Disarm may be beneficial)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:41
#: 153c1724e6a640fbba6498fd51fe6620
msgid ""
"This flight will allow to setup your aircraft in a \"flyable for tuning\""
" state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:43
#: b360d656951441efb5b13c7bc840800b
msgid "Ensure the aircraft is in STABILIZE mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:44
#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:46
#: 924f7beb24994a87801e549c6d8d4128 efbbcf5b9ebb4dc2b035fef9085e7540
msgid "Arm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:45
#: 10a6f310706240a681cd9569a3646479
msgid "Immediately disarm the aircraft to ensure your disarm procedure is correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:47
#: e4eb319e856b4952aa00800271da0e97
msgid ""
"Slowly increase the throttle looking for signs of oscillation. (long or "
"flexible landing gear may cause some landing gear oscillation that will "
"only go away after the aircraft leaves the ground)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:48
#: 201911702a3d49f39f7e49e9747a0c2d
msgid ""
"As soon as the aircraft lifts off the ground immediately put the aircraft"
" back down as gently as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:49
#: ee0a707ac7a647169a1fd4fc1bd627aa
msgid "Disarm the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:50
#: c3834628a6a24150ad20fb83ca264638
msgid ""
"Evaluate what you observed to decide if you need to make adjustments to "
"the tuning parameters or if it is safe to take off again"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:51
#: bf4431d9eeda4b13a9216558e7d600f5
msgid "Arm and increase the throttle to initiate a takeoff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:52
#: 6123eed5f47f4c58b799dd933cf88ded
msgid ""
"Hover at approximately 1m altitude and apply small (5 degrees) control "
"inputs into roll and pitch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:53
#: 416471f3ed8d48aeb7a4e62589029275
msgid "Immediately land if any oscillation is observed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:55
#: 5607854a3fa14fba88fefbd213552948
msgid "Next section will explain how to remove the oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:58
#: c96a313446434cada2ee2907534a22d4
msgid "Initial aircraft tune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:60
#: b46cb5e02fb546b3b0d315dc8181f33a
msgid ""
"The first priority when tuning an multirotor aircraft is to establish a "
"stable tune, free of oscillations, that can be used to do further tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:62
#: eb0a1cb73da142489d315efd060c1993
msgid "Arm the aircraft in STABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:63
#: 97fbf61021d345b582873aebc9f10d0f
msgid "Increase the throttle slowly until the aircraft leaves the ground"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:64
#: ee11fa0dc2b0439fb242aa9ba5588133
msgid ""
"If the aircraft starts to oscillate immediately abort the takeoff and/or "
"land the aircraft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:65
#: 87737e27f9e44593a9f65961fa624d44
msgid "Reduce all the following parameters by 50%"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:67
#: 31ea87ed251d4ff193b301166a2d7468
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_P <ATC_RAT_PIT_P__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:68
#: 445b0e12680e4a40ac02466cb01fd49a
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_I <ATC_RAT_PIT_I__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:69
#: 977e9b59d8454097b1100a51214b5274
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_PIT_D <ATC_RAT_PIT_D__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:70
#: cff8f7864cb94b09b4b3c1c229fdae79
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_P <ATC_RAT_RLL_P__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:71
#: 4a1343e554a9403ab8abd4744bcd2e50
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_I <ATC_RAT_RLL_I__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:72
#: b52d8299748e4077b62408cc351faa7e
msgid ":ref:`ATC_RAT_RLL_D <ATC_RAT_RLL_D__AC_AttitudeControl_Multi>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:74
#: d51bbf63924c47ada44db3def915d504
msgid ""
"This process is repeated until the aircraft can hover without "
"oscillations being detectable visually or audibly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:76
#: 6d06676e282149068911594b774f40f0
msgid ""
"If the aircraft has very long or flexible landing gear then you may need "
"to leave the ground before ground resonance stops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:78
#: ead3991f24cf4820bdd64689358a53ef
msgid ""
"Be aware that in this state the aircraft may be very slow to respond to "
"large control inputs and disturbances. The pilot should be extremely "
"careful to put minimal stick inputs into the aircraft to avoid the "
"possibility of a crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:81
#: 64bbcfb44020452ca37d6ca5bc513555
msgid "Test AltHold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:83
#: 0b2eb734a0024793b51b3708a5ea64ea
msgid ""
"This test will allow to test the altitude controller and ensure the "
"stability of your aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:85
#: e1ca361d2d504750944b36714bb11948
msgid ""
"Check :ref:`MOT_HOVER_LEARN <MOT_HOVER_LEARN>` is set to 2. This will "
"allow the controller to learn by itself the correct hover value when "
"flying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:87
#: f9e84b29c4cf4cb59da37056d89ca6eb
msgid ""
"Take off in STABILIZE and increase altitude to 5m. Switch to AltHold and "
"be ready to switch back to STABILIZE. If the aircraft is hovering at a "
"very low hover throttle value you may hear a reasonably fast oscillation "
"in the motors. Ensure the aircraft has spent at least 30 seconds in hover"
" to let the hover throttle parameter converge to the correct value. Land "
"and disarm the aircraft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:89
#: 497a33bdcec14ced99f66b9fda070527
msgid ""
"Set these parameters on ground and preferably disarm  (A confident pilot "
"could set them in flight with GCS or CH6 tuning knob):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:91
#: cced3a24fd4e4cf7b044d3d7002ce99b
msgid ""
":ref:`PSC_ACCZ_I <PSC_ACCZ_I>` to 2 x :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER "
"<MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:92
#: 97fd3f3918dc4af7ad786f68c39de81d
msgid ":ref:`PSC_ACCZ_P <PSC_ACCZ_P>` to :ref:`MOT_THST_HOVER <MOT_THST_HOVER>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:94
#: b15324e35f4b4618beabb89f4f08e81f
msgid ""
"if AltHold starts to oscillate up and down the position and velocity "
"controllers may need to be reduced by 50%. These values are: "
":ref:`PSC_POSZ_P <PSC_POSZ_P>` and :ref:`PSC_VELZ_P <PSC_VELZ_P>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:97
#: c8cf2c86bf2b410d811e8c37714ff95d
msgid "Harmonic Notch Filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:99
#: fba30bea6918407fa55a8c3554008052
msgid ""
"After you have a hover without oscillations the next step is to get get a"
" good notch filter setup to reduce noise to the  PID controllers. A good "
"set of notch filtering parameters is critical to a good tune."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:104
#: 79610c43f4904c4bbe398a89e7130d92
msgid ""
"To get a notch filter setup you need to hover your vehicle for at least "
"30 seconds with no pilot input and with "
":ref:`INS_LOG_BAT_MASK<INS_LOG_BAT_MASK>` set to 1. This will enable FFT "
"logging which will guide the correct setup of the notch filters. You "
"should then carefully read the :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering` "
"documentation and setup a harmonic notch to remove the noise from your "
"gyros."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/initial-tuning-flight.rst:108
#: 5c14ec6094b74316ac9ac02e00dee1c9
msgid ""
"Eliminating noise with the notch filters will dramatically improve the "
"quality of your tune."
msgstr ""

